00:18:47.146 --> 00:18:48.230
How do I set up clusters?

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:49.349
Why is this so hard?

00:18:49.349 --> 00:18:50.390
How does this stuff work?

00:18:50.390 --> 00:18:52.710
And so it's really nice
to see the reaction

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:54.990
from the Kubernetes
community and the authors

00:18:54.990 --> 00:18:56.240
and the people who work on it.

00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:58.826
Like, coming, OK, yeah, that's
a problem, let's fix it.

00:18:58.826 --> 00:18:59.700
CARTER MORGAN: Right.

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:02.760
Yeah, it's fun, because
Kubernetes is mostly

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:04.017
or largely community-driven.

00:19:04.017 --> 00:19:05.600
When you look at the
number of commits

00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:08.020
