00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:16.815
in the SIGS on the
Git issues, it's

00:19:16.815 --> 00:19:18.190
one of the reasons
why I'm really

00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:19.820
excited about Kubernetes.

00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:20.736
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Cool.

00:19:20.736 --> 00:19:24.777
So these make me think about--
not that long ago, actually, it

00:19:24.777 --> 00:19:26.360
might have been
almost a year already,

00:19:26.360 --> 00:19:31.056
one of our coworkers, Ray Tsang,
created a-- what was the name?

00:19:31.056 --> 00:19:32.680
It was like a mini
cluster, Kubernetes.

00:19:32.680 --> 00:19:34.060
MARK MANDEL: Yeah, he
called it a mini cluster.

00:19:34.060 --> 00:19:35.685
FRANCESC CAMPOY: A
mini cluster, which,

00:19:35.685 --> 00:19:38.060
I don't know if you've seen
