00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:40.210
Pis, one on top of each other.

00:19:40.210 --> 00:19:42.960
So do you think that the
pain he had to go through

00:19:42.960 --> 00:19:47.570
to make Kubernetes run on that
little Raspberry Pi cluster

00:19:47.570 --> 00:19:49.140
could be less now?

00:19:49.140 --> 00:19:55.010
Or how hard or how easy it
is to get Kubernetes cluster

00:19:55.010 --> 00:19:56.639
started outside of GKE?

00:19:56.639 --> 00:19:58.680
CARTER MORGAN: Well,
there's a joke going around,

00:19:58.680 --> 00:20:00.810
